 2026-10-09-revised-para-salary-schedule,2026-10-09,email,"Dr Fortuna, Superintendent",Public records request: revised paraprofessional salary schedule,"The revised paraprofessional salary schedule approved by the School Committee on 7 October 2026, and the paraprofessional agreement (AFSCME Council 93, Local 503) as re-ratified with it, including any memorandum describing the corrections.",The FY26-FY28 agreement and schedule we hold (committed 20 August 2026) are the versions posted before the correction; on 16 September the Superintendent reported that hourly rates did not calculate accurately into annual salaries. Goal: show exactly what changed.,answered,2026-10-09,sources/contracts/pdf/paraprofessional-salary-fy26-fy28-corrected-2026-10-07.pdf; sources/contracts/pdf/paraprofessional-moa-fy26-fy28.pdf; sources/contracts/docx/paraprofessional-wages-draft-union-agreement-2026-09.docx; sources/contracts/docx/paraprofessional-wages-draft-individual-waiver-2026-09.docx; sources/correspondence/2026-09-16-para-wages-superintendent-counsel-payroll.txt (transcription; the .eml held privately),
 2026-10-09-dee-bus-contract,2026-10-09,email,"Dr Fortuna, Superintendent",Public records request: Dee Bus transportation contract,"The current transportation contract between Lunenburg Public Schools and Dee Bus Service with its rate schedule, amendments or extensions, and the contract it replaced; as drafted 9 Oct, also the invitation for bids/RFP and bid response, and the number of buses and routes contracted FY2024-FY2026.","A 7.6% increase in Dee Bus services was cited for FY2026 (Finance Committee, 6 March 2025). To show whether the contract fixes the increase, indexes it, or leaves it to negotiation, and how much is a change in the number of buses (11 regular-education buses per TJ).",answered,2026-10-09,sources/contracts/pdf/dee-bus-transportation-agreement-fy26-fy28.pdf; sources/contracts/pdf/dee-bus-bid-proposal-rates-fy26-fy30.pdf; sources/contracts/pdf/dee-bus-first-amendment-2025.pdf; sources/contracts/pdf/dee-bus-performance-and-payment-bond-fy27.pdf,
 2026-10-19-teacher-step-lane-counts,,email,"Dr Fortuna, Superintendent","Public records request: teachers by step and lane, and the prior teacher agreements","The count of teachers (FTE), by step and lane of the salary schedule, as of 1 October each year FY2018–FY2026 — counts only, no names; and the teacher agreements in force FY2015–FY2024 with their salary schedules.","DESE’s average teacher salary puts Lunenburg second of the six districts this project compares, while residents say its salary schedule is the lowest; both are true if Lunenburg’s teachers sit higher on the scale, and nobody publishes the placement. The town’s own gross wage lists, matched to the school rosters, give a distribution of gross pay (/school-spending-history/teachers-on-the-scale) but cannot separate step, lane, stipends and longevity. The step-and-lane count closes the money-gaps row on teachers by step and lane; the prior agreements close the row on earlier raises (pay-or-headcount). Counts only, so nothing personal is asked for.","drafted, not sent",,,
-2026-10-19-teacher-contract-groton-dunstable,,email,"Superintendent of Schools, Groton-Dunstable Regional School District","Public records request: the current teachers’ collective bargaining agreement, Groton-Dunstable Regional School District","The collective bargaining agreement now in force between the Groton-Dunstable Regional School District school committee and its teachers’ unit (Unit A), including every salary schedule, the longevity provisions and any memoranda of agreement amending it; and, if a successor agreement has been settled but not yet signed, its salary schedules.","This project compares Lunenburg’s teacher salary schedule with the districts it uses for comparison (/school-spending-history/teacher-pay-compared). The only Groton-Dunstable Regional School District agreement it holds is the one DESE publishes, whose salary schedules cover 2017-18 to 2019-20 (Schedule A of the agreement from 1 September 2014) and have expired, so the district cannot be included in a current comparison. The agreement closes the money-gaps row on the current teacher salary schedules of the four districts with none held. A public document; nothing personal is asked for.","drafted, not sent",,,
